    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Develop a correctness-first high-throughput sequential implementation: replace quadratic per-bucket insertion sorting with a stable byte-wise LSD radix sort over the fixed-width strings, and use buffered/fast input and output. Preserve ordinary lexicographic ordering for every valid input, including duplicate keys; do not rely on benchmark-specific distributions. Measure against the 0.4225 s baseline.\",\"B\":\"Investigate a robust comparison-sort alternative: improve parsing/output buffering and sort record pointers/indices with an efficient library or custom comparator sort, optionally retaining independent first-byte buckets only when capacity and ordering are provably safe. Focus on variable/edge string content and exact output correctness rather than assumptions about uniform buckets.\",\"C\":\"Investigate a 4-core parallel design. Partition work without data races, use per-thread histograms/scatter regions or independently sortable ranges, and retain deterministic lexicographic output. Compare OpenMP/parallel radix or parallel sort approaches, accounting for setup and I/O overhead; all valid inputs must remain supported.\",\"G\":\"Integrate and benchmark the strongest complete candidate programs from A/B/C on the supplied correctness suite and timing protocol. Do not assume combined optimizations add speedups: retain only the fastest measured correct whole program. Recheck memory bounds, duplicate handling, declared string-width semantics, buffered final output, and portability on ARM64/4 CPU cores.\",\"analysis\":\"The baseline is correct but spends 0.4225 s using per-bucket insertion sort, which has quadratic worst-case cost and repeatedly invokes strcmp. The source has fixed allocated record stride (declared length plus NUL), so radix sorting is the highest-value route if fixed-width input semantics are honored. Input scanning and one-printf-per-record output are also likely material. Diverse sequential, comparator-based, and parallel research paths reduce risk; integration must select by measurements rather than merge them blindly.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"ba3d7dd77d908ae2390d7e12f42f69587ea9dfb6cb1142973586cf93045731d3\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Develop a correctness-first high-throughput sequential implementation: replace quadratic per-bucket insertion sorting with a stable byte-wise LSD radix sort over the fixed-width strings, and use buffered/fast input and output. Preserve ordinary lexicographic ordering for every valid input, including duplicate keys; do not rely on benchmark-specific distributions. Measure against the 0.4225 s baseline.\",\"B\":\"Investigate a robust comparison-sort alternative: improve parsing/output buffering and sort record pointers/indices with an efficient library or custom comparator sort, optionally retaining independent first-byte buckets only when capacity and ordering are provably safe. Focus on variable/edge string content and exact output correctness rather than assumptions about uniform buckets.\",\"C\":\"Investigate a 4-core parallel design. Partition work without data races, use per-thread histograms/scatter regions or independently sortable ranges, and retain deterministic lexicographic output. Compare OpenMP/parallel radix or parallel sort approaches, accounting for setup and I/O overhead; all valid inputs must remain supported.\",\"G\":\"Integrate and benchmark the strongest complete candidate programs from A/B/C on the supplied correctness suite and timing protocol. Do not assume combined optimizations add speedups: retain only the fastest measured correct whole program. Recheck memory bounds, duplicate handling, declared string-width semantics, buffered final output, and portability on ARM64/4 CPU cores.\",\"analysis\":\"The baseline is correct but spends 0.4225 s using per-bucket insertion sort, which has quadratic worst-case cost and repeatedly invokes strcmp. The source has fixed allocated record stride (declared length plus NUL), so radix sorting is the highest-value route if fixed-width input semantics are honored. Input scanning and one-printf-per-record output are also likely material. Diverse sequential, comparator-based, and parallel research paths reduce risk; integration must select by measurements rather than merge them blindly.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"80ab957e1c82419c918e55f01c53eed4\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"ba3d7dd77d908ae2390d7e12f42f69587ea9dfb6cb1142973586cf93045731d3\",\"session_id\":\"bb34f01e2e114cf4a59ae51b02823166\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"2a0ad46663022c04fc9c4b2a99b4df95a2c2b09cbe04f2c978c7e2e4fbabfeda\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":10279,\"output_tokens\":850,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":462}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":11129,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
